==> kind create cluster --name promptforge-ai
Creates a cluster named promptforge-ai using kind (Kubernetes in Docker).

==> docker compose -f services.docker-compose.yml up
Creates and starts the services defined in the services.docker-compose.yml file.

==> docker build -t promptforge-proxy:latest . || docker build -t promptforge-proxy:latest -f proxy/Dockerfile proxy/
Creates a Docker image named promptforge-proxy:latest using the Dockerfile in the current directory or the proxy directory.

==> kind load docker-image promptforge-proxy:latest --name promptforge-ai
Loads the docker image into promptforge-ai cluster

==> kubectl apply -k .

==> kubectl port-forward svc/redis-service 6379:6379 -n promptforge-apps

==> kubectl port-forward pod/<promptforge-proxy-pod-name> 8090:80 -n promptforge-apps
(optional if we want to port forward the pod to access project from localhost)